{%- comment -%}
  PG Frame Add: the 30x40 black wood frame offered as a paid ADD-ON, the way
  the spare case is on the console page -- on the wall-art product page and in
  the cart -- and NOT as a card in "You may also like".

  Two parts, both DOM-only.

  THERE WAS A THIRD, AND IT IS GONE ON PURPOSE: a tile above ADD TO CART on the
  wall art product page, offering the same frame before the print was even in
  the cart. The shop owner asked for it removed at every width. The cart row
  below is the only place the frame is pitched now, which is the right moment
  for it anyway -- an add-on reads as an add-on once there is something to add
  it to, and on the product page it competed with ADD TO CART for the same
  click. Deleted rather than hidden, so nothing renders and is then covered up:
  its markup, its styling and its `onPrintPage()` guard all went with it.

  If it is ever wanted back, the one trap it was built around is worth knowing:
  its button was `.pgx-frame-add` and deliberately NOT `.pgx-case-add`, because
  pg-mobile and pg-case-add both listen for that class in the CAPTURE phase and
  post the CASE variant -- a shared class would have added a case to the cart
  when the shopper asked for a frame.

  (1) CART. The same offer as one compact light row, shown only while the print
      is in the cart and the frame is not. It lives INSIDE #pg-unlock-slot when
      pg-unlock has built one -- pg-cart-mobile moves that slot above the pinned
      checkout pane on phones, and riding in it is what keeps this row reachable
      there; parked after the line list it measured y=783 on an 844px screen,
      underneath the pane, which is why "they can't add the frame". It still
      does NOT wear the `.pg-unlock` class: pg-unlock's own render sweeps rows
      by that class and removes any it did not ask for, and pg-cart-mobile's
      fallback selector grabs the first one.

  (1b) ONE UPSELL AT A TIME. With the wall art, an orb and a console all in the
      cart, the drawer stacked pg-unlock's three offer rows plus this one --
      four pitches in a row, which reads as clutter and, when two point at the
      same product family, as duplication. focusOne() below keeps exactly one
      of them visible: the frame offer first whenever it is eligible (owner's
      rule: wall art in cart means the frame is the upsell), then the offer for
      the product whose quantity moved most recently, then the slot's own CSS
      order. The losers are benched with a class, not removed -- pg-unlock
      counts its rows to decide whether to rebuild, and removing them would
      make it rebuild forever. A row mid-interaction (is-open, or holding
      focus) is never benched out from under the shopper.

  (2) "YOU MAY ALSO LIKE". The frame card is hidden there, exactly as pg-mobile
      hides the case card -- an add-on and a standalone product card for the
      same thing read as two different offers at two different prices.

  Nothing here polls /cart.js. Whether the print and the frame are in the cart
  is read off the rendered rows, so the offer costs no requests on a cart that
  four other sections are already fetching.

  ================================================================
  WHY THIS ROW LOOKED NOTHING LIKE THE OTHER UPSELLS ON A PHONE

  Reported: with the DUO PACK in the cart the spare-case upsell is bulky and
  cut off, while with a single console the same pitch looks right.

  They are two different components, and only one of them had ever been fixed.
  With ONE console the offer comes from pg-unlock's ladder row (rung 1, "Add a
  2nd R36S") -- the row whose phone geometry was measured and corrected. With
  the DUO PACK that rung is already taken (1 paid + 1 discounted = the 2 in the
  cart), so pg-unlock renders nothing for the console, offer() below sees no
  `.pg-unlock[data-pg-unlock*="handheld-game-console"]` and shows THIS row
  instead. Same pitch, same moment in the cart, different stylesheet -- and this
  one still carried the two faults pg-unlock had already had taken out of it:

  1. `.pg-frameoffer-px` was `white-space:nowrap`, which makes "was + now + SAVE
     chip" one unbreakable unit. On a 390px phone that unit is wider than the
     copy column, so it overflowed and painted UNDER the ADD button -- the
     overlap in the screenshot. pg-unlock's note on its own `-px` rule describes
     the identical failure. The line now breaks BETWEEN its pieces: the struck
     price is nowrap on its own element, the chip is an inline-block, so a
     narrow column drops the chip to its own line instead of running it under
     the button.
  2. The row had no small-phone geometry at all. Its only media block was
     `max-width:480px`, and the one thing it sized -- `.pg-frameoffer-p` -- is a
     class this markup does not contain (the price element is `-px`), so the
     block did nothing but recolour the subtitle. Meanwhile the row sits in
     #pg-unlock-slot, where pg-cart-timer stamps geometry with two-ID
     `!important` rules; with nothing here to answer them the row took whatever
     they gave it.

  So the geometry below is pg-unlock's, restated for this row at the strength
  this slot needs -- `#cart#cart` is three ids, which beats a two-ID !important
  rule whatever the load order, the same trick and for the same reason as
  pg-unlock's own 414px block. The base card also picks up that row's padding,
  radius, gradient and shadow, so the two pitches read as one component whether
  the shopper is holding one console or two.
{%- endcomment -%}
<style>
  /* ---- the cart row ---- */
  /* Geometry, palette and type are pg-unlock's offer row, restated: this row
     and that one are the same pitch in the same slot and must be one design.
     The drawer is light where the product page is dark, so the palette is the
     drawer's, not the tile's. */
  #cart .pg-frameoffer,body.template-cart .pg-frameoffer{
    display:flex;align-items:center;gap:12px;
    /* the price line and, on a narrow phone, the chip must be able to drop to
       their own line rather than overflow the copy column */
    flex-wrap:wrap;
    margin:10px 0 4px;padding:11px 13px;
    border:1px solid rgba(122,47,162,.3);border-radius:14px;
    background:linear-gradient(120deg,#F8F3FC,#F1E7F8);
    box-shadow:0 12px 30px -24px rgba(74,28,102,.45);
    box-sizing:border-box
  }
  #cart .pg-frameoffer img,body.template-cart .pg-frameoffer img{
    width:54px;height:54px;flex:none;border-radius:11px;object-fit:cover;
    background:#efe4f8
  }
  #cart .pg-frameoffer-t,body.template-cart .pg-frameoffer-t{flex:1;min-width:0}
  #cart .pg-frameoffer-t b,body.template-cart .pg-frameoffer-t b{
    display:block;font-size:13.5px;line-height:1.25;color:#3B1553;font-weight:800
  }
  #cart .pg-frameoffer,body.template-cart .pg-frameoffer{font-family:'Poppins','Segoe UI',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif}
  #cart .pg-frameoffer-t small,body.template-cart .pg-frameoffer-t small{
    display:block;font-size:12.5px;line-height:1.35;color:#6E5C80;margin-top:2px
  }
  /* NO `white-space:nowrap` HERE -- see fault 1 in the note above. Each piece
     stays whole on its own element; only the line between them may break. */
  #cart .pg-frameoffer-px,body.template-cart .pg-frameoffer-px{
    display:block;margin-top:3px;font-size:14.5px;font-weight:800;color:#7A2FA2;
    line-height:1.45
  }
  #cart .pg-frameoffer-px s,body.template-cart .pg-frameoffer-px s{
    color:#8a8a8a;font-weight:400;font-size:12px;margin-right:6px;white-space:nowrap
  }
  /* same pill geometry as .pg-unlock-tag: letter-spacing `normal` because
     tracking applies after the final glyph too, leaving a gap no padding can
     balance out */
  #cart .pg-frameoffer-sv,body.template-cart .pg-frameoffer-sv{
    display:inline-block;width:fit-content;margin:0 0 0 8px;
    padding:3px 7px;border-radius:999px;
    font-size:11.5px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:normal;word-spacing:normal;
    text-transform:uppercase;vertical-align:1px;
    color:#fff;background:linear-gradient(120deg,#9B4BC4,#7A2FA2)
  }
  /* ONE SIZE, BESIDE THE COPY AT EVERY WIDTH, and its height comes from
     min-height rather than padding -- padding-derived height put the twin of
     this button at 32px, under the 40px minimum for a tap target sitting above
     CHECKOUT. It was previously declared twice here, in two blocks that
     disagreed about padding and font-size. */
  #cart .pg-frameoffer-add,body.template-cart .pg-frameoffer-add{
    flex:0 0 auto;order:0;
    display:inline-flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;
    min-height:34px;line-height:1;white-space:nowrap;
    border:0 !important;
    background:linear-gradient(120deg,#B478E0 0%,#9B4BC4 35%,#7A2FA2 70%,#4A1C66 100%) !important;
    color:#fff !important;
    box-shadow:0 10px 22px -12px rgba(139,68,190,.7) !important;
    border-radius:999px !important;padding:0 16px !important;
    font-family:inherit;font-weight:800;font-size:12.5px;
    letter-spacing:.06em;text-transform:uppercase;cursor:pointer
  }
  html body #cart .pg-frameoffer-add::before,html body #cart .pg-frameoffer-add::after{
    display:none !important;content:none !important;background:none !important
  }
  #cart .pg-frameoffer-add[disabled]{opacity:.6;cursor:default}
  /* Inside the slot the row goes FIRST -- the slot is a CSS-ordered flex
     column, and every pg-unlock row already carries an explicit order, so the
     frame offer takes a rank below them all. */
  #cart #pg-unlock-slot .pg-frameoffer{order:99}

  /* The bench. Hidden, not removed: pg-unlock decides whether to rebuild by
     COUNTING its rows, so a removed row would be rebuilt on the next pass and
     the drawer would churn. display beats the slot's flex layout either way. */
  #cart .pg-upsell-bench,body.template-cart .pg-upsell-bench{display:none !important}

  /* ---- PHONES (max-width:600px) ----
     pg-unlock's mobile-parity block, restated: the row keeps the same three
     parts in the same order at every width -- image, copy, button, all on one
     line. The button deliberately does NOT go full-width here; that is what
     made the twin of this row a 322x42 slab on a 390px phone. */
  @media (max-width:600px){
    #cart .pg-frameoffer,body.template-cart .pg-frameoffer{gap:11px}
    #cart .pg-frameoffer img,body.template-cart .pg-frameoffer img{width:48px;height:48px}
    #cart .pg-frameoffer-t b,body.template-cart .pg-frameoffer-t b{font-size:14px}
    #cart .pg-frameoffer-t small,body.template-cart .pg-frameoffer-t small{font-size:11.5px}
  }

  /* ---- SMALL PHONES (max-width:414px) ----
     iPhone 13/16/17 at 390-402px land here. pg-cart-timer's compact block
     stamps rows in this slot with TWO-ID !important rules (38x38 thumbnails,
     every text node at 12px) and loads after this file, so at equal specificity
     it wins. `#cart#cart` is three ids and wins at any load order -- the same
     answer pg-unlock's own 414px block gives, so the two rows end up identical
     rather than merely similar. Thumbnail stretched to the row's height, button
     compact so the copy keeps the line width, and the SAVE chip gives up its
     slack before the line has to wrap. */
  @media (max-width:414px){
    #cart#cart .pg-frameoffer img{
      width:46px !important;height:auto !important;min-height:52px !important;
      align-self:stretch !important
    }
    #cart#cart .pg-frameoffer .pg-frameoffer-add{
      min-height:30px !important;padding:0 11px !important;font-size:12px !important
    }
    #cart#cart .pg-frameoffer .pg-frameoffer-px .pg-frameoffer-sv{
      padding:2px 5px !important;margin-left:6px !important;font-size:10.5px !important
    }
    #cart#cart .pg-frameoffer .pg-frameoffer-t b{font-size:13.5px !important;line-height:1.3 !important}
    #cart#cart .pg-frameoffer .pg-frameoffer-t small{font-size:11px !important}
    #cart#cart .pg-frameoffer .pg-frameoffer-px{font-size:14px !important}
  }
</style>
<script>
(function(){
  if (window.pgFrameAdd) return; window.pgFrameAdd = 1;

  /* Both accessory upsells share this one row builder: the frame rides with
     the wall art, the spare case with the console. Prices are the LIVE ones -
     was = the variant's compareAtPrice - so the strike and the SAVE % are the
     same maths the cart itself shows. */
  var ACCS = [
    {
      key: 'frame',
      variant: 49688364613860,
      ownMark: '30x40cm-frame',
      withMark: 'lenticular-poster',
      img: 'https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0815/5706/1860/files/blackframe_120x.png?v=1787284280',
      title: 'Add the matching frame',
      each: 'Add a frame for each print',
      sub: '30x40cm black wood grain',
      now: 1499, was: 2799
    },
    {
      key: 'case',
      variant: 49640879063268,
      ownMark: 'r36s-protective-case',
      withMark: 'handheld-game-console',
      img: 'https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0815/5706/1860/files/hf_20260810_234744_eb2ec102-427d-4c23-94f0-453e70014817.png?v=1786422962&width=120',
      title: 'Add a spare protective case',
      each: 'Add a spare case for each console',
      sub: 'One case already comes free',
      now: 1399, was: 2499
    }
  ];
  window.pgAccFor = function(handle){
    var h = String(handle || '');
    for (var i = 0; i < ACCS.length; i++){ if (h.indexOf(ACCS[i].withMark) > -1) return ACCS[i]; }
    return null;
  };
  function moneyC(c){ return '$' + (c / 100).toFixed(2); }
  var FRAME_MARK = '30x40cm-frame';   /* still referenced by the YML trim below */

  /* ---------------- (1) the cart row ---------------- */
  function cartLines(){
    return document.querySelectorAll('#cart .l4ca:not(.in-panel) > li, body.template-cart .form-cart .l4ca:not(.in-panel) > li');
  }
  function cartHas(mark, paidOnly){
    var ls = cartLines();
    for (var i = 0; i < ls.length; i++){
      if (!ls[i].querySelector('a[href*="' + mark + '"]')) continue;
      /* paidOnly skips the auto-added FREE gift line - the spare-case offer
         must still show while only the free case is in the cart */
      if (paidOnly && ls[i].hasAttribute('data-pg-free')) continue;
      return true;
    }
    return false;
  }
  function offer(){
    var list = document.querySelector('#cart .l4ca:not(.in-panel), body.template-cart .form-cart .l4ca:not(.in-panel)');
    ACCS.forEach(function(cfg){
      /* one row per accessory, ever */
      var rows = document.querySelectorAll('.pg-frameoffer[data-acc="' + cfg.key + '"]');
      var row = rows[0] || null;
      for (var i = 1; i < rows.length; i++){
        if (rows[i].parentNode) rows[i].parentNode.removeChild(rows[i]);
      }
      var wanted = !!list && cartHas(cfg.withMark) && !cartHas(cfg.ownMark, true) &&
        !document.querySelector('#cart .pg-unlock[data-pg-unlock*="' + cfg.withMark + '"]');
      if (!wanted){
        if (row && row.parentNode) row.parentNode.removeChild(row);
        return;
      }
      var save = Math.round((cfg.was - cfg.now) / cfg.was * 100);
      if (!row){
        row = document.createElement('div');
        row.className = 'pg-frameoffer';
        row.setAttribute('data-acc', cfg.key);
        row.innerHTML =
            '<img alt="" width="54" height="54" decoding="sync" src="' + cfg.img + '">'
          + '<div class="pg-frameoffer-t"><b>' + cfg.title + '</b>'
          + '<span class="pg-frameoffer-px"><s>' + moneyC(cfg.was) + '</s>' + moneyC(cfg.now)
          + '<span class="pg-frameoffer-sv">SAVE ' + save + '%</span></span>'
          + '<small>' + cfg.sub + '</small></div>'
          + '<button type="button" class="pg-frameoffer-add" data-v="' + cfg.variant + '">Add</button>';
      }
      var slot = document.querySelector('#cart #pg-unlock-slot');
      if (slot){
        if (row.parentNode !== slot) slot.appendChild(row);
      } else if (row.previousElementSibling !== list || row.parentNode !== list.parentNode){
        list.parentNode.insertBefore(row, list.nextSibling);
      }
    });
  }

  /* ---------------- (1b) one upsell at a time ----------------
     Candidates are the frame offer plus every pg-unlock row. The winner:
       1. any row the shopper is interacting with (open picker / focus)
       2. the frame offer, whenever it is on screen at all -- offer() has
          already established eligibility by then
       3. the row for the product whose cart quantity changed most recently
       4. the slot's own CSS order
     Everyone else gets the bench class. */
  var lastTouched = '', prevQty = null;
  function trackTouch(){
    var q = {};
    document.querySelectorAll('#cart .l4ca:not(.in-panel) > li').forEach(function(li){
      var a = li.querySelector('a[href*="/products/"]');
      if (!a) return;
      var m = (a.getAttribute('href') || '').match(/\/products\/([^/?#]+)/);
      if (!m) return;
      var inp = li.querySelector('input[type=number]');
      q[m[1]] = (q[m[1]] || 0) + (inp ? (parseInt(inp.value, 10) || 0) : 1);
    });
    if (prevQty){
      for (var h in q){
        if (!(h in prevQty) || q[h] > prevQty[h]) lastTouched = h;
      }
    }
    prevQty = q;
  }
  function focusOne(){
    /* Benching is OFF by request: each product in the cart shows its next
       bundle up, and the poster/console additionally show their accessory
       (frame / spare case). The bench class is only cleared now. */
    var cands = [];
    document.querySelectorAll('#cart .pg-unlock, #cart .pg-frameoffer').forEach(function(el){
      cands.push(el);
    });
    cands.forEach(function(el){ el.classList.remove('pg-upsell-bench'); });
    if (true) return;
    if (cands.length < 2){
      cands.forEach(function(el){ el.classList.remove('pg-upsell-bench'); });
      return;
    }
    var winner = null, i, el;
    for (i = 0; i < cands.length && !winner; i++){
      el = cands[i];
      if (el.classList.contains('is-open') || el.contains(document.activeElement)) winner = el;
    }
    if (!winner){
      for (i = 0; i < cands.length && !winner; i++){
        if (cands[i].classList.contains('pg-frameoffer')) winner = cands[i];
      }
    }
    if (!winner && lastTouched){
      for (i = 0; i < cands.length && !winner; i++){
        if (cands[i].getAttribute('data-pg-unlock') === lastTouched) winner = cands[i];
      }
    }
    if (!winner){
      var best = null;
      for (i = 0; i < cands.length; i++){
        var o = parseInt(getComputedStyle(cands[i]).order, 10) || 0;
        if (best === null || o < best){ best = o; winner = cands[i]; }
      }
    }
    cands.forEach(function(c){ c.classList.toggle('pg-upsell-bench', c !== winner); });
  }

  /* ---------------- adding it ---------------- */
  /* Capture phase, delegated: the row above is re-created by the sweep below
     whenever the drawer rebuilds, so a listener bound to the button itself
     would not survive; and the drawer's own handlers call stopPropagation on
     clicks inside it. */
  var busy = false;
  document.addEventListener('click', function(e){
    var btn = e.target && e.target.closest && e.target.closest('.pg-frameoffer-add');
    if (!btn) return;
    e.preventDefault();
    e.stopPropagation();
    if (busy) return;
    busy = true;
    var was = btn.textContent;
    btn.textContent = 'ADDING...';
    fetch('/cart/add.js', {
      method: 'POST',
      headers: {'Content-Type': 'application/json'},
      credentials: 'same-origin',
      body: JSON.stringify({items: [{id: parseInt(btn.getAttribute('data-v'), 10) || 49688364613860, quantity: 1}]})
    }).then(function(r){
      if (!r.ok) throw 0;
      btn.innerHTML = 'ADDED ✓';
      if (window.pgDrawerRefresh){
        try { return Promise.resolve(window.pgDrawerRefresh()); } catch(err){}
      }
    }).then(function(){
      /* the pgOpenCart() call that used to live here belonged to the product
         page tile -- adding from the cart means the cart is already open */
      setTimeout(function(){ busy = false; offer(); }, 400);
      setTimeout(function(){ btn.textContent = was; }, 2200);
    }).catch(function(){
      /* reverting silently to ADD reads as a dead button -- say it failed */
      btn.textContent = 'TRY AGAIN';
      setTimeout(function(){ btn.textContent = was; }, 2000);
      busy = false;
    });
  }, true);

  /* ---------------- (2) out of "You may also like" ---------------- */
  function ymlTrim(){
    document.querySelectorAll('.pgu-yml a, .pgu-yml-grid a').forEach(function(a){
      if ((a.getAttribute('href') || '').indexOf(FRAME_MARK) > -1){
        var card = a.closest('.pgu-yml-card') || a;
        card.style.setProperty('display', 'none', 'important');
      }
    });
  }

  function pass(){ offer(); trackTouch(); focusOne(); ymlTrim(); }

  /* Event-driven, with a slow backstop -- the drawer rebuilds on every cart
     change and fires no event this section can subscribe to. Nothing in the
     pass touches the network. */
  if (window.MutationObserver){
    var t = null;
    new MutationObserver(function(){
      if (t) return;
      t = setTimeout(function(){ t = null; pass(); }, 120);
    }).observe(document.body, {childList: true, subtree: true});
  }
  setInterval(pass, 1500);
  if (document.readyState === 'loading') document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', pass);
  else pass();
})();
</script>
{% schema %}
{"name": "PG Frame Add", "settings": []}
{% endschema %}
